1111.3083	open_problem	When {{formula:f6ec2250-483d-4a11-84c2-8181dab177e2}} , both the A- and B-modes contribute in an optimal way to the grains radial motion.	Values of {{formula:fb5e0f0e-e509-42e9-9b18-9365e1842f44}} and {{formula:aa4f7362-3fea-4d89-81ce-e8d8f6315f71}} in the {{formula:4ff2ca04-e27c-4087-a9cb-ddf10e568201}} plane are shown in Fig. REF . When {{formula:f6ec2250-483d-4a11-84c2-8181dab177e2}} , both the A- and B-modes contribute in an optimal way to the grains radial motion. In this case, grains can be efficiently accreted by the central star if {{formula:47c1ae11-d66b-4271-8aec-a6733cc074ca}} . Thus, they can not contribute to the formation of pre-planetesimals. This process is called the radial-drift barrier for planet formation.	0.8
